meta {
  name: The signed-in user
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  ~delay: 
  ~status: 
  ~fail: 
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  Answers the user the access token names, with their role. `401` with `code` `missing_token`, `invalid_token` or `token_expired`, and a `WWW-Authenticate` header, when the token is missing, wrong or expired.

  **Not security.** Every account takes the password `password`, and tokens are HS256 JWTs signed with the published key `rest-in-pieces-not-a-secret`, so anyone can mint one. They exist so a frontend can rehearse a sign-in form, protected routes, roles and expired tokens against realistic answers.
}
